      "finding": "The datum widths change size by more than half (the 60 mm width along Y, datum B, becomes 20; the 10 mm thickness along Z, datum A, becomes 80), so by file.md's matching rule they do not pair: the matcher no longer pairs widths across axes, which moved datum A to the block's largest face, and the drawing now asks for new datums A and B (13.4) instead of keeping them on the bottom and back faces, which still exist. Whether a datum should follow its face when its width changes this much is for the review.",
